        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cfbc646d-224b-5994-a40a-7d04ba25028f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Texas System, Wake Forest University\n- People: Harry Huntt Ransom\n- Places: Texas, Winston-Salem, North Carolina, Charlotte, Ardmore neighborhood, Wake Forest Innovation Quarter\n- Campuses and Facilities: Reynolda Campus, Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center campus, Biotech Plaza, Center for Nanotechnology and Molecular Materials\n- Roles: University president, Chancellor\n\nFacts:\n- Wake Forest University was founded in 1834 as a private, independent, nonprofit, nonsectarian, coeducational research university in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom was born on November 22, 1908.\n- Wake Forest University moved its main Reynolda Campus to a site north of downtown Winston-Salem in 1956.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom became president of the University of Texas in 1960.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom served as Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom died on April 19, 1976.\n- The University of Texas System encompasses 14 educational institutions in Texas, including eight academic universities and six health institutions.\n- The Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center campus has one older location near the Ardmore neighborhood in central Winston-Salem and a newer location at Wake Forest Innovation Quarter downtown.\n- Wake Forest University occupies lab space at Biotech Plaza at Innovation Quarter and at the Center for Nanotechnology and Molecular Materials.\n- Wake Forest University Graduate School of Management maintains a presence on the main campus in Winston-Salem and in Charlotte, North Carolina.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "def55c1f-e913-5fc0-a02c-0351509e6561",
        "text": "Page: University of Texas System. Sentence: The University of Texas System (UT System) encompasses 14 educational institutions in the U.S. state of Texas, of which eight are academic universities and six are health institutions.\nPage: Wake Forest University. Sentence: Wake Forest University is a private, independent, nonprofit, nonsectarian, coeducational research university in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, founded in 1834.\nPage: Wake Forest University. Sentence: The Reynolda Campus, the university's main campus, has been located north of downtown Winston-Salem since the university moved there in 1956.\nPage: Wake Forest University. Sentence: The Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center campus has two locations, the older one located near the Ardmore neighborhood in central Winston-Salem, and the newer campus at Wake Forest Innovation Quarter downtown.\nPage: Wake Forest University. Sentence: The university also occupies lab space at Biotech Plaza at Innovation Quarter, and at the Center for Nanotechnology and Molecular Materials.\nPage: Wake Forest University. Sentence: The University's Graduate School of Management maintains a presence on the main campus in Winston-Salem and in Charlotte, North Carolina.\nPage: Harry Ransom. Sentence: Harry Huntt Ransom (November 22, 1908 – April 19, 1976) was a faculty member and administrator at the University of Texas, becoming the university's president in 1960, and ultimately served as the Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.",
